<title>UK: Rolls-Royce up as SBC Warburg says oversold.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce up as SBC Warburg says oversold.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Rolls-Royce Plc rose on Wednesday as analysts at SBC Warburg said the stock was oversold, market sources said.</p>
<p>Rolls shares were up 4p at 225-1/2 in active trade of 3.7 million shares, rebounding from the seven-month low of 217-1/2p set February 17.</p>
<p>In a review of the engineering sector, SBC Warburg also highlighted TI Group Plc, GKN Plc, Smiths Industries Plc and Glynwed Plc, sources said.</p>
<p>Analysts at the brokerage were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
